var e=[{question:`Can Fern maintain my existing docs where they are?`,answer:`No. Fern verifies and updates articles that live in Ferndesk. You import your existing help center (URLs preserved, redirects created, usually under ten minutes), and from then on she keeps it accurate. Your support tool stays where it is, and Fern keeps reading tickets from it.`},{question:`What does “verified” actually mean?`,answer:`Fern checks every claim she can test against your product: navigation steps, setting names, feature behaviour, screenshots, API shapes. Claims she can’t check against a source, like pricing policy or third-party behaviour, are flagged, not guessed.`},{question:`How often does verification run?`,answer:`Monthly on every plan, plus any time you click Verify. Pull requests are checked as they merge, so new releases don’t wait for the monthly pass.`},{question:`What if Fern gets something wrong?`,answer:`Nothing publishes without you. Every drifted article comes back as a draft with the changes highlighted. Approve, edit or dismiss.`},{question:`Will my URLs break when I import?`,answer:`No. Original paths are preserved and 301 redirects are created for anything that changes. Sitemap and canonical tags are handled.`},{question:`Is my codebase safe?`,answer:`Ferndesk never stores your source. Fern reads repositories through GitHub with read-only access, and only when you ask her to check or draft.`},{question:`What if we’re not on GitHub?`,answer:`Fern verifies against your live website, your support tickets and any other source you connect. GitHub gives the most precise results.`},{question:`Can I use my own domain?`,answer:`Yes. Point help.yourcompany.com at Ferndesk, or serve it from yourcompany.com/help to keep the SEO on your main domain.`},{question:`Is there a free trial?`,answer:`Every plan starts with 7 days free and full access, no card required. Most teams have their help center live within the hour.`},{question:`What if I leave?`,answer:`Every article is yours at any time: export the whole help center as markdown in a zip, or pull it through the API. You’re never locked in.`}],t=[{question:`How does the AI write articles?`,answer:`Fern connects to your codebase, support tickets, videos, and changelogs to understand your product. When you ask her to write an article, she drafts content based on real product context, not generic AI filler. You review and approve everything before publishing.`},{question:`What if the AI writes something incorrect?`,answer:`Nothing publishes without your approval. Fern drafts articles and suggests updates, but you're always in control. Think of her as a very fast first-draft writer who knows your product inside and out.`},{question:`What are automatic PR screenings?`,answer:`When you merge a pull request, Fern automatically screens the change and drafts any doc updates it needs, so your docs keep up with your code. Pro screens every PR you merge, with no monthly cap, and manual drafting with AI is always unlimited.`},{question:`How many AI conversations do I get?`,answer:`A conversation is one exchange between a user and Fern in your help center, counted once however many questions it runs to. Pro includes 1,000 a month and Enterprise includes 2,500. Need more? Add 500 any time for $25.`},{question:`How do I migrate my existing help center?`,answer:`We offer one-click migration from Intercom, Zendesk, HelpScout, and more. Your URLs are preserved with automatic redirects, so you won't lose SEO rankings or break existing links. Need a custom migration? We'll handle it for you, free of charge.`},{question:`Can I use my own domain?`,answer:`Yes. You can connect a custom domain (help.yourcompany.com) or host your help center on a subfolder of your main site (yourcompany.com/help) for maximum SEO benefit.`},{question:`Is my codebase safe?`,answer:`Ferndesk doesn't keep a copy of your codebase. Fern only reads your repositories, through our GitHub App, and never writes to them. While she works on a task, she uses a temporary private copy on our servers that is deleted about 30 minutes after she last uses it. The only code we keep is the snippets she looked at, saved in that task's history so you can see how she reached her answer. We never use your code to train AI models.`},{question:`Do you offer SSO and enterprise security?`,answer:`Pro includes private, authenticated help centers for internal documentation, with SSO, OpenID Connect and magic links. Enterprise adds SAML SSO and SCIM provisioning for automatic user management, plus custom integrations. We also offer a data processing agreement (DPA).`},{question:`Is there a free trial?`,answer:`Yes. Pro starts with a 7-day free trial and full access to every feature, no credit card required. Add your card any time to keep going when the trial ends. Most customers have their help center live within an hour.`},{question:`Can I switch between monthly and yearly?`,answer:`Yes. There is one plan, so the only choice is how you pay for it. Switch to yearly any time and two months are free; the change is prorated. Switch back to monthly and it takes effect at your next billing date.`},{question:`How many people can I add to my team?`,answer:`Pro includes 5 seats. Need more? Add seats any time for $10 each per month.`},{question:`Why switch from Intercom/Zendesk/HelpScout?`,answer:`Traditional help desk tools treat documentation as an afterthought. Ferndesk is built for self-service first, with AI that actually keeps your docs current, blazing-fast performance for better SEO, and a modern editor that's a joy to use.`},{question:`What integrations do you support?`,answer:`We integrate with GitHub, Linear, Slack, Intercom, Zendesk, Notion, and 10+ other tools. Fern can read from these sources to draft articles and keep content in sync. Enterprise plans can request custom integrations. <a href="/integrations" class="underline underline-offset-2">See all integrations</a>.`}];export{e as n,t};